\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Lowest eigenvalue of the clamped unit-square membrane (\code {Quad4Laplace}), consistent against lumped mass: the relative error in absolute value. The consistent-mass eigenvalue is above the exact one and the lumped-mass eigenvalue is below it. Produced by \texttt {scripts/ch03\_assets.py}.\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.31}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces The mechanism of shear locking in a bilinear element under bending (schematic). The exact bending mode curves the edges and has no shear strain; the bilinear interpolation keeps the edges straight, which produces a parasitic shear strain and an artificially stiff element.\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.34}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces Pure bending of a plane-stress beam, tip deflection divided by the exact value, against the number of elements along the beam. The quadratic elements are exact on these meshes. The helper is the one used by \texttt {fea\_engine/tests/test\_benchmarks\_convergence.py}.\relax }}{21}{figure.caption.36}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.5}{\ignorespaces Convergence of the first cantilever frequency of the Euler--Bernoulli beam (left) and of the tip deflection of the Reissner beam (right) with the element size, with the observed order.\relax }}{23}{figure.caption.44}%
