\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces The model problem on a $40\times 40$ mesh ($1521\xspace $ unknowns). Left: displacement with the contact set outlined; right: contact force $\bm {\lambda }$, which is zero outside the contact set. The solver finds $295\xspace $ active constraints in $12\xspace $ iterations. Produced by \texttt {scripts/ch07\_assets.py}.\relax }}{54}{figure.caption.99}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Penalty against exact contact on the model problem ($841\xspace $ unknowns). Left: the largest penetration falls like $1/k_p$ but never reaches zero; the exact solution has no penetration (drawn at the plotting floor). Right: the condition number of the penalty matrix grows in proportion to $k_p$; the exact route solves a system whose condition number does not depend on any parameter.\relax }}{55}{figure.caption.100}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.3}{\ignorespaces Left: the complementarity condition (red) against a penalty law (blue, dashed), which lets the gap become negative. Right: the active-set iteration in four steps.\relax }}{56}{figure.caption.105}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.4}{\ignorespaces The active-set iteration on the model problem with $N=1521\xspace $ unknowns. Left: the number of active constraints per iteration for the \texttt {reduced} and \texttt {saddle} routes (the curves coincide). Right: the number of constraints that changed status; the last point (plotted at 0.5) is zero changes, which is the stopping test.\relax }}{57}{figure.caption.106}%
