\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.1}{\ignorespaces The six levels of evidence used in this book. Lower levels contain many small cases and are cheap to repeat; higher levels contain few cases and test more of the stack at once. A higher level does not replace a lower one: it can pass while a component below it is wrong in a region it does not visit.\relax }}{140}{figure.caption.246}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.2}{\ignorespaces Flat beam of \citet {he2023mfsnlrom}. (a) Centre displacement over $\pm 2000$\nobreakspace {}Pa: nonlinear FE, multi-fidelity surrogate and ICE ($R^2=1.0000\xspace $ and $1.0000\xspace $ against FE). (b) Free decay of the first modal coordinate ($R^2=0.9971\xspace $ for case a and $0.9899\xspace $ for case b). (c) Backbone by harmonic balance against FE free vibration; largest frequency error $0.96\,\%\xspace $ over a hardening of $21.9\,\%\xspace $ above the linear frequency. One surrogate evaluation takes $5.0\times 10^{-5}$\xspace {}\nobreakspace {}s against 0.84\xspace {}\nobreakspace {}s for FE, a ratio of $1.7\times 10^{4}$\xspace . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{144}{figure.caption.249}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.3}{\ignorespaces Free-vibration check of the hybrid ROM of \citet {yang2019hybrid}: frequency relative to the linear one, full-order model against ROM. (a) Cylindrical panel: the ROM follows the softening and hardening, with a largest frequency error of 0.087\,\%\xspace . (b) Plate with a hole: the ROM hardens about 4.9\xspace {} times too much at the largest amplitude. Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{144}{figure.caption.250}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.4}{\ignorespaces One-mode ICE ROM against the full-order model for the flat beam of \citet {hollkamp2008ice}: displacement at $x=4$\nobreakspace {}in over the first $0.2$\nobreakspace {}s and its power spectral density, at the low level (RMS error 19.5\,\%\xspace ) and the high level (RMS error 136\,\%\xspace ). Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{145}{figure.caption.251}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.5}{\ignorespaces Moving-load beam of \citet {liang2024fdpinn}. (a) Normalised error of the band-limited field against the band width, full-order sweep; the cost of the 5\nobreakspace {}Hz band is $3.8\times 10^{-5}$\xspace , $5.6\times 10^{-6}$\xspace {} and $4.0\times 10^{-6}$\xspace {} for the three cases. (b) The same error from frequency-domain ROMs of size $r$; with ten modes they agree with the full-order value to within 0.05\,\%\xspace . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{146}{figure.caption.252}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.6}{\ignorespaces Greedy loop for the rope problem of \citet {fauque2018hybrid}, best run. (a), (b) Error of the hybrid (HR, hyper-reduced) and projection-based (PB) reduced models against the iteration (displacement mean 0.011\,\%\xspace {}, maximum 0.084\,\%\xspace {}; contact force on the reduced domain 0.45\,\%\xspace {} mean, reconstructed force 10\,\%\xspace {} mean at the end). (c) Size of the reduced problem. Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{147}{figure.caption.253}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.7}{\ignorespaces 2D assembly of \citet {nikiema2026assembly}, plain Newton. (a) Error of the last increment for the four reduced models at three tolerances; crosses mark runs that did not converge (DEIM and UDEIM at $\varepsilon =10^{-6}$). (b) Converged runs: error against the number of elements evaluated per iteration. POD error at $\varepsilon =10^{-5}$: 0.94\,\%\xspace . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{148}{figure.caption.254}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.8}{\ignorespaces Dynamic obstacle problem of \citet {balajewicz2016contact} (1\,521 dofs). (a) Maximum error against the greedy iteration for the three indicator weightings and the true-error oracle (a reduction of 288\xspace {} for $\alpha =(1,0,0)$). (b), (c) Response at a test parameter: the NMF dual basis follows the full-order model (error 0.083\,\%\xspace ), the SVD dual basis does not (error 307\,\%\xspace ). Measured speed-up 14.7\xspace . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{149}{figure.caption.255}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.9}{\ignorespaces Neural operator of \citet {yang2025frino}: mean relative error for single tones at low and high frequency, multi-frequency loads and random loads, for three training sets. Dashed lines are the publication's values. With 40 tones the multi-frequency and random errors are 0.443\xspace {} and 0.691\xspace . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{149}{figure.caption.256}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.10}{\ignorespaces The integrated pipeline. Blue: \texttt {fea\_engine}{}; violet: \texttt {rom\_engine}{}; grey: data; green: checks. The basis size is chosen on a validation set of the training kind; the two test sets are used once, at the end.\relax }}{151}{figure.caption.258}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.11}{\ignorespaces (a) Largest error against the basis size $r$ on the validation set and the two test sets (small mesh): the full state, and for set\nobreakspace {}B also the peak stress; the horizontal line is the tolerance and the vertical line the chosen $r$. (b) Online residual indicator against the true error of the full state for the 80 test queries. (c) Time per query on the small mesh.\relax }}{152}{figure.caption.261}%
